From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bluefin Server maintainers <noreply@projectbluefin.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] go-source: update to go1.27.2

freedesktop-sdk 26.08.2 (and its release/26.08 branch and master at the
time of writing) builds Go from go1.27.1. Go 1.27.2 is a security
point release; the fix that matters for this image is

  GO-2026-6607 / CVE-2026-97031 crypto/tls: a crafted ClientHello with
  repeated ECH outer-extension references makes a TLS server amplify
  memory while parsing the hello (memory exhaustion), fixed by
  rejecting the malformed encoding.

homelab/bluefin-cluster.bst builds the homelab join service with
components/go.bst. `bluefin-cluster serve` is a crypto/tls server
(internal/join/server.go: tls.NewListener + HandshakeContext) that
listens on every interface and advertises itself over DNS-SD, and the
handshake runs before the passphrase (PAKE) check, so an unauthenticated
LAN peer reaches the affected parser.

The 1.27.2 tree is otherwise the same where FSDK touches it:
src/internal/buildcfg/exp.go (patches/go/disable-dwarf5.patch) is
byte-identical between go1.27.1 and go1.27.2, so the FSDK patch queue
still applies. Drop this patch when the junction moves to an FSDK tag
whose go-source.yml is at go1.27.2 or later.

Ref: https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6607
Ref: https://go.dev/issue/81855
---
 elements/include/go-source.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/elements/include/go-source.yml b/elements/include/go-source.yml
index c5c005f..ec5283a 100644
--- a/elements/include/go-source.yml
+++ b/elements/include/go-source.yml
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ sources:
   exclude:
   - '*rc*'
   - '*beta*'
-  ref: go1.27.1-0-g862c888e612ac346c7c4d99c9392bdfd265f33b0
+  ref: go1.27.2-0-g022c8636110ebac86a9b88724cda168ed713c21f
 - kind: patch
   path: patches/go/disable-dwarf5.patch
 
